      "problem": "Evaluate $1+(2-3x)$ for $x=-1.$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $x$ with $-1$ in the expression and evaluate the parentheses first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+(2-3x) & = \\\\ 1+(2-3\\cdot (-1)) & = \\\\ 1+(2-(-3)) & = \\\\ 1+(2+3) & = \\\\ 1+5 & = \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}\n$$",
